Optimization after #7: initramfs settle caps 20s -> 10s in init-top/udev,
   init-bottom/udev, and functions; initramfs regenerated and verified.
   Expected kernel time ~30s instead of ~56s (total ~55s). To be validated by
   one more cold boot (Linux poweroff -> button).

Validation:
  10s build: SUCCESS, 59.677s (kernel 35.641s + userspace 24.022s), SSH ~40s.
  Then caps reduced to 3s (init-top, init-bottom, functions) and rebuilt.
  Final cold boot 2026-11-21 01:59:56: SUCCESS, SSH up in 38s,
  systemd-analyze 38.677s (kernel 14.740s + userspace 23.937s), single udevd.
  => 9/9 clean cold boots total (7 in the requested series + the 10 s and 3 s
     validation boots). The first post-fix boot also succeeded but had the
     duplicate-hook mistake and is counted separately.

Cleanup done:
  - extlinux loglevel reverted 6 -> 1 (takes effect next boot).
  - temporary /etc/systemd/system.conf.d/10-watchdog.conf removed;
    RuntimeWatchdogUSec=0.
  - temporary NOPASSWD sudo rule removed; verified SUDO_NEEDS_PASS.
  - /var/tmp extraction dirs cleaned; /var/tmp/fix-initrd.{sh,log} and
    /var/backups/opirv2-udevfix kept for reference.
  - Rootfs is 90% used (6.2G free) - worth watching.
Remaining, by user's choice: reboot is not fixed (warm reset wedges the SD
